Z||000000||jhogans||10-17-1999||11:11 PM||||I was checking out the Customer Car Section of V8 Archies - <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/customer.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/customer.htm</A>  - and I came upon this kick-ass looking notchback - <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/wade.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/wade.htm</A>  -<P>I've seen pictures of notchbacks but I have never seen one that looked like this.  The picture is a side-view but it has ground effects like a Fastback.  Is there a particular Fiero that looks like this or did this guy add ground effects.  <P>Is that a hood scoop on the guys trunk?  Where can you get one like that?  What about that spoiler?  <P>This guy has one tight ride.<P>Thanks for any info guys.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||10-17-1999||11:22 PM||||Looks to me to be an '85? SE or GT.  Note the indented Pontiac logo on the rear, and also the designation on the quarter windows.  My bets guess is that it's an '85 GT.  But, if it is, he also added a high mount brake light (dole light).  Only on '86 and later Fiero's.  It can't be the stock yellow from '88 since that rear fascia is clearly not from an '88.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-17-1999).]||||reg||1
