Z||000010||batboy||10-20-1999||08:26 PM||||SCCA Fiero, I'm honored that you remembered I have a 87 SE with a 4 banger. DJRice, there were only 1,401 made like my car and only 2,474 SE Fieros with V6's in 1987. Kind of rare, but not really worth a lot, at least right now.<P>If you guys can see SE lettering on the quarter windows, your eyesight is better than mine. Assuming the third brake light is original and it is a SE model, it has to be a 86 or 87 model. Yes, the ground effects are factory on SE for those years, except they were normally painted a contrasting color (black on my silver 87 SE). ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Patrick||10-21-1999||03:19 AM||||<BR>Ummmm.... I'm no expert, but I believe that the Fiero pictured up above is NOT an '87. The '87 and '88 Fieros have a recessed area in their bumpers that are <B>wider</B> than the reflectors are in the back. You'll notice that this Fiero has reflectors that sit in recesses that are only as big as the reflectors are.<P>Hey, I could be wrong...||||reg||4
