Z||000017||fiero56||10-22-1999||09:27 AM||||The way I remember it is: the '87-'88 coupe, along with the formula had the longer reflectors in back, while the '86 to '87 SE's had the rear fascia like the '85 GT.Kinda confusing to read.  <BR>Have you uys ever heard of Mark Corbin? He sells a Fiero spotters guide for 4 bucks, plus $1 shipping.  I bought one off him at the FOCOA nationals here in columbus a few months ago.  It has all production numbers, options, what came standard with what, percentages, paint options, interior options, everything.  It also shows what years and models came with what front and rear fascias. It is the most complete guide I have found yet. If you need his address to order one, I can look it for you. Have to find the guide, I *think* it's in my Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Greg Piet||10-23-1999||02:18 AM||||I have an 85 SE, and my rear bumper fascia has two black "bumpers".  These are physical raises in the fascia.  I dont see these on the yellow car above...  So if its and 85 then it has replaced the fascia (Or mine had its fascia replaced with an 84 rear bumper fascia)||||reg||1
Z||000019||batboy||10-23-1999||07:54 AM||||Greg, you're right about the black raised bumpers on the 85 SE (the Batmobile is also a 85 SE and has those too), but the 86 and 87 SE models had the same nose and tail as the 85 GT (looks just like that picture). But, the 85 GT did not have a third brake light and it had GT on the quarter windows instead of SE. I can't think of a single difference between the 86 and 87 SE models.||||reg||1
