Z||000032||Fab4mula||10-25-1999||11:38 PM||||Ok, let's look at this for a minute.  The rear bumper is clearly 85GT.  The recessed Pontiac lettering tells you that.  The sil panel windows (hard to make out) appear to have SE on them.  Then there's the 3rd brake light wich would put it in the 86+ category.  Finally you have the SMOOTH body moulding around the car.  This was 86+ I believe.  The 84-85 has a black moulding that is ribbed (thin rib on top, wide rib in middle, thin rib on bottom).<P>The car appears to be a combination of parts.  I'd have to believe that the basis was an 86+ car, since not many people I can think of would go through the trouble of putting the 3rd brake light in after the fact.  Who really knows what it was.  Anyone got the VIN#?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
